      "message": "NOTE: I am not sure if we should also check TRBLIMITR_EL1_XE. I considered being cautious and preemptively checking it, but after a closer check, I found that it\u0027ss currently not used by the kernel, and none of the bits that are related with TRBE_ENABLED are coupled to this bit. In other words, this behavior matches how non-protected mode handles this.\n\n\nhttps://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0487/maa/-Part-D-The-AArch64-System-Level-Architecture/-Chapter-D24-AArch64-System-Register-Descriptions/-D24-4-Trace-registers/-D24-4-3-TRBLIMITR-EL1--Trace-Buffer-Limit-Address-Register",
